hadiths[200]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1001","It is narrated from the freed slave of the Prophet (peace be upon him), Sayyiduna Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him), that indeed the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a man is deprived of sustenance because of the sin which he commits."
"1002","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, there are some servants of Allah such that if they swear an oath by Allah (that Allah will do something), Allah certainly fulfills their oath."
"1003","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said . . . . . . and he narrated a hadith similar to this."
"1004","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said . . . . . . and he narrated a hadith similar to this."
"1005","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, there are some servants of Allah who recognize people by their signs."
"1006","This hadith is also narrated through another chain from Ibrahim bin Abdullah al-Mukharmi with his chain in the same manner, but in it, instead of «حدثنا ثابت» , there is «عن ثابت» ."
"1007","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, among the servants of Allah are those whom He has created for fulfilling the needs of people; people turn to them in their needs with anxiety, and these are the ones who will be safe on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"1008","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, among Allah’s servants are those whom He has created for fulfilling people’s needs; people turn to them in times of difficulty, and these are the ones who will be safe on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"1009","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, raced with a man and the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, outran him. The Muslims were very pleased at this. Then that man said to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: ""O Messenger of Allah! (Let us) race again."" The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Yes."" So he raced with him (again), and that man outran the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. This was displeasing to the Prophet and his companions. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Indeed, it is Allah's way that whatever thing He raises in the world, He also brings it down."
"1010","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Indeed, replying to a letter is as necessary as replying to a greeting (salam)."" The Shaykh says: Its chain of narration is not strong."
"1011","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, there is protection from lying in speaking with hints and allusions."
"1012","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Prophet (peace be upon him) that he said: ""Indeed, the best thing a person eats is that which is from his own earnings, and his children are also from his own earnings."
"1013","This hadith is also narrated through another chain from Ali bin Abdul Aziz with his chain in the same manner."
"1014","Sayyiduna Hubshi bin Junadah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say in a lengthy hadith: ""Indeed, asking is only permissible for a person who is extremely needy or one who is burdened under the weight of debt."
"1015","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): O Messenger of Allah! Which deed is the best? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""Knowledge."" He said: O Messenger of Allah! I am asking you about action, while you are telling me about knowledge? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a little action with much knowledge is plentiful, and much action with ignorance is little."
"1016","It is narrated from Abu Zahriyah that a man asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him: ""Tell me the most virtuous deed."" The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said to him: ""Adhere to knowledge."" Upon this, he said: ""I have asked you about the most virtuous deed?"" The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said to him: ""Adhere to knowledge, for even a little action with much knowledge is abundant, and much action with ignorance is little."" This narration is also reported through another chain."
"1017","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a servant (because of good character) attains the rank of the fasting person and the one who stands (in prayer) at night, who fasts all day and stands (in prayer) all night."
"1018","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, every religion has a characteristic, and indeed the characteristic of this religion is modesty.”"
"1019","Yazid bin Talha bin Rukanah narrates this as a marfu’ (elevated) tradition, and in it is: “Indeed, every religion has a characteristic, and the characteristic of Islam is modesty.”"
"1020","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, everything has an honor, and indeed the most honorable gathering is that by which one turns towards the Qiblah."
"1021","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, everything has an honor, and indeed the most honorable gathering is that by which one turns towards the Qiblah, and indeed your gatherings should be conducted with trustworthiness."
"1022","Sayyiduna Ka'b bin 'Iyad (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Indeed, every nation has a trial, and indeed the trial of my nation is wealth."
"1023","Sayyiduna Ka'b bin 'Iyad (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say this... and he narrated this hadith."
"1024","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Indeed, every nation has a trial, and indeed the trial of my nation is wealth."
"1025","Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) says that one day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to us. He (peace be upon him) held both doorposts of the mosque and called out in a loud voice: ""O people! O people of Islam! Death has come with that which it was to come with; it has come to the friends of Allah, who are among the people of the Abode of Joy, whose striving and desire is to dwell therein, with comfort, mercy, and a blessed return. O people! O people of Islam! Death has come with that which it was to come with; it has come to the friends of Satan, who are among the people of the Abode of Deceit, whose striving and desire is to dwell therein, with regret, remorse, and a wretched return. Listen! Every striver has a limit, and the limit of every striver is death."
"1026","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said . . . . . . and he narrated a hadith in which it was also mentioned: ""Indeed, for every doer there is enthusiasm (in action), and for every enthusiasm there is a period of slackness."
"1027","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had some freed slaves who used to fast continuously and stand in prayer at night. It was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so he said: ""Indeed, for every doer of deeds there is enthusiasm, then for that enthusiasm there is a period of slackening."
"1028","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) while he was reclining. He said: ""Mu'adh! In what state did you begin your morning?"" He replied: ""I began my morning with faith in Allah."" He said: ""Indeed, every statement has a confirmation and every truth has a reality."" And he narrated a lengthy hadith."
"1029","Sayyiduna Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, every king has a protected pasture, and indeed the protected pasture of Allah is that which He has declared unlawful.”"
"1030","Aamir Sha’bi says that I heard Sayyiduna Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) saying this, and he narrated a long hadith in which it was also mentioned: “Listen! Every king has a specific sanctuary. Listen! The specific sanctuary of Allah is that which He has forbidden.”"
"1031","Harith bin Ubaidah reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Indeed, every fasting person has an (accepted) supplication, and when he intends to break his fast, he should recite this supplication at the time of his first morsel: O Possessor of vast forgiveness! Forgive me."
"1032","Zamrah bin Habib reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Indeed, everything has a door, and indeed the door of worship is fasting.”"
"1033","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), from Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), who narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, everything has a mine, and the mine of piety is the hearts of the people of gnosis."
"1034","Salim bin Abdullah narrates from his father (Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him) who said that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Indeed, everything has a mine, and the mine of piety is the hearts of the people of gnosis."
"1035","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, everything has a heart, and indeed the heart of the Qur'an is Surah Ya-Sin. So whoever recites Surah Ya-Sin, for him, because of reciting it, the reward of reciting the Qur'an ten times will be written."
"1036","Sayyiduna Ubayy ibn Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, everything has a heart, and indeed the heart of the Qur'an is Surah Yasin. Whoever recites Surah Yasin seeking the pleasure of Allah, Allah will forgive him, and he will receive a reward as if he has recited the entire Qur'an twelve times. And for any Muslim in whose presence Surah Yasin is recited at the time of the descent of the Angel of Death, for every letter of this Surah, ten angels will descend who will stand in rows before him, send blessings upon him, seek forgiveness for him, be present at the time of his washing, walk with his funeral, perform the funeral prayer, witness his burial. And any Muslim who recites Surah Yasin in the throes of death, the Angel of Death will not seize his soul until the guardian angel of Paradise, 'Ridwan', brings him the drink of Paradise, which he will drink while still on his bed. Then the Angel of Death will seize his soul while he is satiated, and he will remain satiated in his grave, and on the Day of Resurrection he will be raised in a state of satiation, and he will not be in need of any of the basins of the noble Prophets (peace be upon them) until he enters Paradise, and he will be satiated."
"1037","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, every prophet has a (granted) supplication. And indeed, I have kept my supplication hidden for intercession on behalf of my ummah on the Day of Resurrection."" Muslim ibn Hajjaj has also narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) with his chain that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said . . . . . . and he narrated this hadith."
"1038","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every prophet has a supplication which he makes for his ummah, and indeed I have reserved my supplication for intercession on behalf of my ummah on the Day of Resurrection."
"1039","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, every prophet has a supplication, and I, if Allah wills, intend to conceal my supplication for intercession on behalf of my Ummah on the Day of Resurrection."" In Ibn Marzuq's narration, the words are «لكل نبي» ""for every prophet."
"1040","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I said to Ka'b al-Ahbar: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every prophet has a supplication which he makes, but I intend to conceal my supplication for intercession on behalf of my ummah on the Day of Resurrection."" So Ka'b said to Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him): Did you hear this hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)? Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: Yes."
"1041","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""Every prophet has a supplication which, when he makes it, is accepted, and I intend to reserve my supplication for interceding on behalf of my ummah in the Hereafter."
"1042","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every prophet has a supplication, and I, insha’Allah, intend to keep my supplication hidden to intercede for my ummah."
"1043","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, every prophet has a supplication which he makes for his ummah, and indeed I have kept my supplication hidden for interceding on behalf of my ummah."
"1044","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every prophet has a supplication which he makes, and indeed I have reserved my supplication for interceding on behalf of my Ummah on the Day of Resurrection."
"1045","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Every prophet has a supplication, and I, insha’Allah, intend to keep my supplication hidden so that I may intercede for my ummah on the Day of Resurrection."
"1046","Arthi says that we went to visit Sayyiduna Khabbab (may Allah be pleased with him) when he was ill, and a wall was being constructed in his house. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: ""Indeed, a believer is rewarded for all his expenses except for what he spends on mud or building construction."
"1047","Abdur Rahman bin Ka'b bin Malik narrates from his father that he said: I asked: O Messenger of Allah! What do you think about poetry? The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a believer strives with his sword and his tongue. By Him in Whose hand is my soul, it is as if he strikes them with spears (through satire)."
"1048","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, envy consumes good deeds just as fire consumes wood."
"1049","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, envy consumes good deeds just as fire consumes wood."
"1050","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Do you know what thing will cause most people to enter Hell?” The Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) said: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “Indeed, the thing that will cause most people to enter Hell is the two hollow things: the mouth and the private parts. Do you know what thing will cause most people to enter Paradise?” The Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) said: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, the thing that will cause most people to enter Paradise is the fear of Allah and good character.”"
"1051","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the religion began as something strange, and soon it will return to being strange just as it began, so glad tidings to the strangers."
"1052","Kathir bin Abdullah Muzani narrates from his father, who narrates from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Indeed, the religion began as something strange, and soon it will return to being strange just as it began, so glad tidings are for the strangers."" It was asked: O Messenger of Allah! Who are the strangers? He said: ""Those who revive my Sunnah and teach it to the servants of Allah."
"1053","Kathir bin Abdullah narrates from his father, who narrates from his grandfather, that indeed the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Verily, Islam began as something strange, and soon it will become strange again just as it began, so glad tidings are for the strangers."" It was asked: O Messenger of Allah! Who are the strangers? He said: ""Those who will revive my Sunnah and teach it to the servants of Allah."
"1054","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Islam began as something strange, and it will soon return to being strange just as it began, so glad tidings are for the strangers."
"1055","Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa’d Sa’idi (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, Islam began as something strange, and soon it will return to being strange just as it began, so glad tidings are for the strangers.” It was asked: O Messenger of Allah! Who are the strangers? He said: “Those who will rectify (the Sunnahs) when people corrupt them.”"
"1056","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a tribulation will arise that will uproot the servants, but the scholar will be saved from it because of his knowledge."
"1057","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the evil eye causes a man to enter the grave and a camel to enter the cooking pot."
"1058","This hadith is also narrated from Shu'ayb through another chain with his chain in the same manner."
"1059","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul, surely the evil eye causes a man to enter the grave and a camel to enter the cooking pot."
"1060","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, whoever drags his garment out of arrogance, then on the Day of Resurrection Allah Almighty will not even look at him."" And in the narration of Abu Muhammad from Abdullah bin Dinar, (instead of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him) it is Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
"1061","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, whoever drags his garment out of arrogance, Allah Almighty will not even look at him on the Day of Resurrection."" This hadith is concise."
"1062","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, whoever drags his garment out of arrogance, Allah will not even look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"1063","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah loves gentleness in every matter."
"1064","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said . . . . . . and she narrated this hadith."
"1065","It is narrated from Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that a group of Jews came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) . . . . . . and they narrated this hadith and said that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Aisha! Indeed, Allah loves gentleness in every matter."
"1066","It is narrated from Ibn Shihab that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Indeed, Allah loves gentleness in every matter."" Imam Muslim has also narrated it with his chain from Imam Zuhri with his chain in the same manner."
"1067","Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, Allah is beautiful and loves beauty, and He also loves to see the effect of His blessing upon His servant, and He dislikes affliction and showing poverty.”"
"1068","Ubaidullah bin Saeed bin Katheer bin Afeer reports that his father Saeed narrated from his father, who narrated from his grandfather, that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah is beautiful and loves beauty."" Muslim has also narrated it with his chain from our master Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), who narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and he has narrated it in a brief form."
"1069","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah loves those who persist in supplication."
"1070","This narration is also reported in the same way from Kathir bin Ubaid through another chain, and in it is «عن النبی صلی اللہ علیہ وسلم» ."
"1071","Zaid bin Aslam narrates from his father that Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) (one day) went towards the Prophet’s Mosque and saw that Sayyiduna Mu’adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) was crying at the grave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He said: “Mu’adh! Why are you crying?” He replied: “What makes me cry is what I heard from the one in this grave. I heard him say: ‘Indeed, Allah loves the righteous, unknown, pious people who, when absent from gatherings, are not sought after, and when present, are not recognized or called upon (even though) their hearts are lamps of guidance; they emerge safely from every dusty, dark trial.’”"
"1072","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah loves a believing person who earns a livelihood."
"1073","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, loves the one who adopts a profession."
"1074","This narration is reported with these words through another chain: ""Indeed, Allah loves a believing person who adopts a profession."
"1075","Sayyiduna Abu Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, Allah loves every sorrowful heart.”"
"1076","Sayyiduna Husayn ibn Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah loves lofty and elevated deeds, and dislikes lowly deeds."
"1077","Sayyiduna Ali bin Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, loves lofty and noble character and dislikes lowly character."
"1078","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah loves that His concession be accepted just as He loves that His disobedience be abandoned."
"1079","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty likes that His (given) concession be accepted just as He likes that His resolute commands be accepted."" She says: I asked: O Messenger of Allah! Which are His resolute commands? He said: ""His obligations."
"1080","Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) held the end of my turban and said: ""O Imran! Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, loves spending and does not love withholding, so spend and be generous, and do not keep the mouth of your bag tied, otherwise seeking (provision) will become difficult for you. And know that indeed Allah loves the discerning eye at the time of desires and the perfect intellect at the time of doubts descending, and He also loves generosity even if it is over a few dates, and He loves bravery even if it is in killing a snake."
"1081","Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) held the end of my turban from behind and then said: ""O Imran! Indeed, Allah loves spending and does not love withholding, so (you yourself) eat and (also) feed others, and do not tie up the mouth of your bag, otherwise seeking (provision) will become difficult for you. And know that indeed Allah loves the discerning eye at the time of desires and the perfect intellect at the time of doubts descending, and He also loves generosity even if it is over a few dates, and He also loves bravery even if it is in killing a snake."
"1082","Sayyiduna Aswad bin Sari’ (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, your Lord loves praises.” The narrator has reported it in brief."
"1083","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah loves gentleness and graciousness."
"1084","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah loves gentleness and graciousness."
"1085","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ubadah bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Surely Allah accepts His servant's repentance until the time when the rattling (of the throat) begins (i.e., until the state of death overtakes him)."
"1086","This narration is reported from Abu Asim Nahdi that indeed Allah Almighty dislikes a powerful mischievous person who has not been afflicted by any calamity in his body or wealth."
"1087","It is narrated from Yahya bin Abi Kathir that indeed the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Surely Allah has disliked for you idle deeds during prayer, obscene speech while fasting, and laughing near graves."
"1088","Warrad says that Sayyiduna Mughirah bin Shu’bah (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote a letter to Sayyiduna Mu’awiyah (may Allah be pleased with him). He was dictating to me and I was writing with my own hand that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Verily, Allah forbids you from idle talk, wasting wealth, and asking too many questions.”"
"1089","Sha'bi says that the scribe of Sayyiduna Mughirah bin Shu'bah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to me, he said that Sayyiduna Mu'awiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote a letter to Sayyiduna Mughirah bin Shu'bah (may Allah be pleased with him) asking him to write and send a hadith which he had heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). So he wrote to him: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Indeed, Allah has disliked three things for you: idle talk, wasting wealth, and asking too many questions."
"1090","Sayyiduna Ammar bin Yasir and Mughirah bin Shu'bah (may Allah be pleased with them) report that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah has disliked for you excessive questioning, wasting wealth, not giving yourself and taking from others, burying daughters alive, and disobeying the mother."
"1091","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah has a sense of honor for the Muslim, so he (the Muslim) should also have a sense of honor."
"1092","This hadith is also narrated through another chain from Uthman bin Abdullah with his chain in a similar manner."
"1093","Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Indeed, Allah shows mercy only to those among His servants who are merciful."
"1094","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Indeed, Allah removes seventy evil deaths because of charity."
"1095","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Indeed, Allah benefits the servant even because of the sin that he commits."
"1096","Sayyiduna Nu’man bin ‘Amr bin Muqarrin (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, Allah will support this religion even through a wicked person.”"
"1097","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that we participated in the Battle of Khaybar along with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he mentioned this hadith at length, and at the end of it were these words: ""Only a Muslim person will enter Paradise, and indeed Allah will support this religion even through a wicked person."
"1098","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, Allah is pleased with the servant who, when he eats food or drinks a beverage, praises Allah for it.” This has also been narrated by Muslim ibn al-Hajjaj with his chain, and in it is: “Whoever eats food and praises Him (Allah) for it, or drinks a beverage and praises Him (Allah) for it.”"
"1099","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, Allah is pleased with the servant who, when he eats food, praises Allah for it, or when he drinks a drink, praises Allah for it.”"
"1100","Abu Ahwas narrates from his father that he presented himself before the Prophet (peace be upon him), and the Prophet (peace be upon him) said to him: ""Indeed, when Allah bestows a blessing upon a servant, He likes to see its effect on him."" The narrator has reported this concisely."
"1101","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah likes to see the effect of His blessing upon His servant, and He dislikes misery and showing poverty."
"1102","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) that he once went out wearing a silk handkerchief (shawl). (Before this) he had never been seen wearing such (expensive) clothing. When people objected to this, he said: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah bestows a favor upon a servant, He likes that its effect be seen on him."" Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah al-Hafiz says: Shuba took two hadiths from this shaykh (Mufaddal bin Fadala), and to our knowledge, no one except Shuba narrated from him. There was no close relationship between them, because (Shuba) was from Basra and Mufaddal was from Hijaz, and be certain that Shuba is unique in narrating from several (shaykhs); no one except Shuba narrated from these (shaykhs)."
"1103","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah will not take away knowledge by snatching it from the people, but He will take away knowledge by taking away the scholars (from the world)."
"1104","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said . . . . . . and he narrated this hadith and in it he said: ""Indeed, Allah will not take away knowledge by snatching it from His servants."
"1105","This hadith is also narrated from Hisham through another chain with his chain in the same manner."
"1106","This hadith is also narrated from Hisham through another chain with his chain in the same manner."
"1107","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah will not take away knowledge by snatching it from the people, but He will take away knowledge by taking away the scholars (from the world). Then, when no scholar remains, people will take the ignorant as leaders; they will be asked and will give verdicts without knowledge. Thus, they will go astray themselves and will lead others astray as well."
"1108","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Indeed, Allah grants the world for the intention of the Hereafter, but He refuses to give the Hereafter for the intention of the world."
"1109","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Indeed, Allah grants the world for the intention of the Hereafter, but He refuses to give the Hereafter for the intention of the world."
"1110","Sayyiduna Salman al-Farsi (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah is shy from His servant that he (the servant) raises his hands towards Him and He (Allah) returns them empty."
"1111","Sayyiduna Salman al-Farsi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, your Lord is Most Modest and Generous. He feels shy from His servant when he raises his hands towards Him to return them empty."
"1112","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Indeed, Allah has made the entire earth a mosque and a means of purification for me."
"1113","Sayyiduna Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed Allah,"" or he said: ""Indeed my Lord, folded the earth for me so that I saw its eastern and western extents, and indeed the dominion of my Ummah will reach as far as it was folded for me."
"1114","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Indeed, Allah has pardoned my Ummah for whatever thoughts arise in their hearts, as long as they do not speak about them or act upon them."
"1115","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Verily, Allah has pardoned my Ummah for all those things that arise in their hearts as long as they do not speak about them or act upon them.” Muslim has also narrated it with his chain from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, Allah has pardoned my Ummah for all those things that arise in their hearts as long as they do not speak about them or act upon them.”"
"1116","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Indeed, Allah has placed comfort and happiness in contentment and certainty through His justice and fairness, while He has placed grief and distress in doubt and displeasure."" The narrator is in doubt about the word ""happiness or ease"" (as to which of these words was actually stated)."
"1117","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah has made jealousy obligatory upon women and modesty obligatory upon men. So whoever among them is patient with the intention of reward, for him is the reward equal to that of a martyr."
"1118","Umar bin Dharr narrates from his father, who said that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Indeed, Allah is near the tongue of every speaker, so a servant should fear Allah and see what he is saying."
"1119","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty does not accept the deed of a servant until He is pleased with his speech."
"1120","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when Allah the Exalted intends good for a people, He puts them to trial."
"1121","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Indeed, the greatest reward comes with the greatest trial, and indeed, when Allah the Mighty and Majestic loves a people, He puts them to trial. Then whoever is content (with the trial), for him is pleasure, and whoever is displeased, for him is displeasure."
"1122","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection, the severest punishment among the people will be for that scholar whose knowledge did not benefit him from what Allah had given him.”"
"1123","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Indeed, the worst person in the sight of Allah on the Day of Resurrection will be the one whom people avoid meeting because of his obscene speech."" There is an incident in this narration which I have summarized."
"1124","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that a man sought permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, he is a bad man of his tribe."" Then when he entered, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) spoke to him openly and cheerfully. When he left, another man sought permission. When he sought permission, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""He is a good man of his tribe."" Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says: When that man entered, you did not speak to him openly as you had spoken to the first one, nor did you show him such cheerfulness. She says: When he left, I said: O Messenger of Allah! You said what you said about so-and-so, then you spoke to him openly and cheerfully, and you said what you said about the other, but I did not see you treat him in that way? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Aisha! Indeed, the worst person among people is the one whom people avoid because of his foul language."
"1125","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the worst person among the people in the sight of Allah Almighty is the one who ruins his Hereafter for the sake of someone else's worldly life."
"1126","Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Indeed, among the wretched, the greatest wretch is the one upon whom the poverty of this world and the punishment of the Hereafter are combined.” This hadith is concise."
"1127","Sayyiduna Amr bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Indeed, I fear three things for my Ummah after me: the slipping of a scholar, an oppressive ruler, and the following of desires."
"1128","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I am grabbing hold of your waists, preventing you from (falling into) Hell, and you are falling into it just as moths and rain insects fall into the fire."
"1129","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I am holding onto your waists, preventing you from the Hellfire, and you are falling into it just as moths and rain insects fall into the fire."
"1130","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), who said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I am holding your waists, keeping you away from the Fire, but you are forcefully falling into it just as moths and rainy season insects fall into the fire. Soon your waists will be let go, and (listen) I will be your forerunner at the Hawd (Pond) of Kawthar. There you will come separately and together; I will recognize you by your marks and names just as a man recognizes a strange camel among his own camels (with ease). And you will be taken to the left side. I will plead to the Lord of the worlds about you, saying: O my Lord! These are my people, O my Lord! These are my people. Then it will be said: Indeed, you do not know what innovations they introduced after you. Indeed, after you, they kept turning back on their heels (from the religion). (Listen!) I will surely recognize among you the person who will come on the Day of Resurrection carrying a bleating goat, and he will call out: O Muhammad! O Muhammad! I will say: I can do nothing for you; I had conveyed (the message of Allah). And I will surely recognize among you the person who will come on the Day of Resurrection carrying a bellowing camel, and he will call out: O Muhammad! O Muhammad! But I will say: I can do nothing for you; I had conveyed (the message of Allah). And I will surely recognize among you the person who will come on the Day of Resurrection carrying a neighing horse, and he will call out: O Muhammad! O Muhammad! But I will say: I can do nothing for you; I had conveyed (the message of Allah). And I will surely recognize among you the person who will come on the Day of Resurrection carrying a water-skin, and he will call out: O Muhammad! O Muhammad! But I will say: I can do nothing for you; I had conveyed (the message of Allah)."
"1131","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah knows about everything He has declared unlawful that surely someone among you will look into it. Beware! Indeed, I am holding your waists to prevent you from falling into the Fire (and you are falling) like moths and rain insects fall into the fire."
"1132","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, my example and your example is like that of a person who kindled a fire, and when it lit up what was around him, moths and other creatures that fall into the fire began to fall into it. So I am holding you back from falling into the fire by grasping you by your waists, but you are slipping from my hands and falling into it."
"1133","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Muawiyah bin Humaidah (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What is the matter with me that I am grabbing you by your waists, saving you from the Fire?"
"1134","Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I went to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and two men from the Ash‘ari tribe were with me. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Musa!"" or he said: ""O Abdullah bin Qais! Indeed, we do not appoint to our work the one who desires it."
"1135","Abu Qatadah and Abu Dahma say that we came to a Bedouin man, and he said that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, took my hand and taught me those things which Allah Almighty had taught him. So among the things that I remembered from what I heard from him, one was this: ""Indeed, whatever you leave out of fear of Allah, Allah will grant you something better than it."
"1136","This hadith is also narrated through another chain from Humaid bin Hilal with his chain in the same manner, but in it, this hadith is narrated from Abu Qatadah and Abu Bilal, and they also mentioned the name of that man."
"1137","Humaid bin Hilal narrates from a man, who said that I presented myself before the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), a pulpit was placed for you whose legs were of iron, I memorized what you taught me, you said: ""Indeed, whatever you leave for the sake of seeking Allah's pleasure, Allah will grant you something better in its place."
"1138","Humaid bin Hilal narrates from the person who either asked the Prophet (peace be upon him) or heard from him. He said: I presented myself before the Prophet (peace be upon him) while he was delivering a sermon. I said: Teach me from the knowledge that Allah has granted you. The Prophet (peace be upon him) descended (from the pulpit), and a chair made of palm bark with iron legs was placed for him. Then he said: ""Indeed, whatever you leave for the sake of Allah out of fear of Him, Allah will grant you something better in its place."" Rifaa’ah ‘Adawi (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I presented myself before the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) while he was delivering a sermon. I said: O Messenger of Allah! I am a stranger, I have come to ask you about the religion, I do not have knowledge about the religion. He says that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) descended (from the pulpit), interrupted his sermon, then a chair made of palm bark with iron legs was brought, and he began to teach me what Allah Almighty had taught him. Then he (again) ascended the pulpit for his sermon."
"1139","Sayyiduna Hasan bin Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, bringing happiness to your Muslim brother is among the deeds that make forgiveness obligatory.”"
"1140","Miqdam bin Shurayh narrates from his father, who narrates from his grandfather, he said: I asked: O Messenger of Allah! Which deed is it that will admit me to Paradise? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “Indeed, spreading peace and speaking good words are among the actions that make forgiveness obligatory.”"
"1141","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the world is very sweet and green, and indeed Allah Almighty will make you successors in it to see how you act. Therefore, beware of the world and beware of women, and there is no word superior to the word of truth spoken before a tyrant ruler."
"1142","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) led us in the 'Asr prayer, then he stood up to deliver a sermon. In his sermon, he said: ""Listen! Indeed, the world is very sweet and lush, and indeed Allah will make you successors in it to see how you act."" This has also been narrated by Muslim ibn al-Hajjaj with his chain of transmission."
"1143","It is narrated from Sayyida Khawla bint Qais (may Allah be pleased with her) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and our master Hamza (may Allah be pleased with him) spoke about the world, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the world is very sweet and green, so whoever takes from it according to his need, blessing will be placed in it for him."
"1144","Sayyida Umrah bint Harith bin Abi Dhirar (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the world is lush and sweet, so whoever receives something from its lawful portion, then that is the thing in which he will be blessed. And how many are there who misuse the wealth of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, and His Messenger; for them, on the Day of Resurrection, there is fire."
"1145","It is narrated from Ali bin Rabah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Indeed, in every valley of the heart of the son of Adam there is a branch. So whoever's heart inclines towards every valley, Allah does not care in which valley He destroys him."
"1146","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... ""Indeed, the most blessed among the women of my Ummah is she whose face is pleasant and whose dowry is small."
"1147","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with both of them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, this religion is very strong, so enter into it gently, and do not make your soul averse to the worship of Allah, for the one who drives a fast mount can neither cover the (whole) journey of the land nor does he let the mount survive.”"
"1148","This hadith is also narrated from Abu Yahya through another chain with his chain in the same manner."
"1149","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, it is from the Sunnah that a person accompanies his guest to the door when bidding him farewell."
"1150","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... (He narrated similar to the first hadith.)"
"1151","1151 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Umar al-Bazzaz narrated to us, Ibn al-A’rabi narrated to us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz informed us, Abu Ubaid narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Isma’il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from Zubayd al-Yami, from someone who informed him from Abdullah ibn Mas’ud, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: « إِنَّ رُوحَ الْقُدُسِ نَفَثَ فِي رُوعِي أَنَّ نَفْسًا لَنْ تَمُوتَ حَتَّى تَسْتَكْمِلَ رِزْقَهَا، فَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ وَأَجْمِلُوا فِي الطَّلَبِ »"
"1152","1152 - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Udfuwi informed us, (he said): Abu al-Tayyib Ahmad ibn Sulayman al-Jurayri granted permission, (he said): Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Jarir al-Tabari narrated to us, (he said): Ali ibn Sahl al-Ramli narrated to me, (he said): Hajjaj, meaning ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, (he said): Ibn Jurayj said: Abu al-Zubayr said: Jabir said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: « أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ إِنَّ أَحَدَكُمْ لَنْ يَمُوتَ حَتَّى يَسْتَكْمِلَ رِزْقَهُ، وَلَا تَسْتَبْطِئُوا الرِّزْقَ، وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ، وَأَجْمِلُوا فِي الطَّلَبِ، وَخُذُوا مَا حَلَّ وَذَرُوا مَا حَرُمَ »"
"1153","1153 - Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Hakim al-Uruzzi informed us, Isma'il ibn Ya'qub ibn al-Jirab narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Maslamah al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Abu Mas'ud, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: « إِنَّ مِمَّا أَدْرَكَ النَّاسُ مِنْ كَلَامِ النُّبُوَّةِ الْأُولَى إِذَا لَمْ تَسْتَحِ فَاصْنَعْ مَا شِئْتَ »"
"1154","1154 - And I am Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Musa al-Simsar, (who said): I was told by Abu Zayd, who said: I was told by al-Farabrī, who said: I was told by al-Bukhari, who said: Adam narrated to us, who said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, who said: I heard Rib'i ibn Hirash narrating from Abu Mas'ud, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: « إِنَّ مِمَّا أَدْرَكَ النَّاسُ مِنْ كَلَامِ النُّبُوَّةِ إِذَا لَمْ تَسْتَحِ فَاصْنَعْ مَا شِئْتَ »"
"1155","1155 - And narrated by Abu Muhammad al-Tujibi, narrated to us Ibn Jami', narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Maslamah al-Qa'nabi, with his chain, the like of it."
"1156","Sayyiduna Abu Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, from what the people have obtained of the words of the first Prophethood is this: If you feel no shame, then do whatever you wish.”"
"1157","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the (true) worshipper knocks at the door of the King, and it is a fact that whoever continuously knocks at the door, it is near that it will be opened for him."
"1158","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, there is engagement in prayer."
"1159","Ibn Aisha (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from his father, who said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said while delivering a sermon: ""Indeed, my Lord has commanded me that my speech should be remembrance, my silence should be reflection, and my looking should be a source of lesson."
"1160","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am but a mercy sent (by Allah Almighty)."
"1161","This narration is also reported from A‘mash through his chain in another way in the same manner, and in it is: ""O people! I am a mercy sent (by Allah, the Exalted)."
"1162","Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, asking (about an issue) is the cure for ignorance.”"
"1163","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), and he related this hadith in detail, and in it was also that this matter reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""They killed him, may Allah destroy them! When they did not know the ruling, why did they not ask? Surely, asking is the cure for ignorance."
"1164","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that once the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was sitting in the mosque and his companions were surrounding him, when suddenly Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) came and stood, greeted with salam, and then began to look for a suitable place to sit. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) began to look at the faces of his companions to see who would make space for him. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) was sitting to the right of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him); he moved from his place and said, ""Abu al-Hasan! Sit here."" So he sat between the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him). Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I saw happiness on the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), then he turned towards Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: ""Abu Bakr! Only the people of virtue recognize the rank of those who possess virtue."
"1165","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been sent only to perfect noble character."
"1166","Sayyiduna Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I fear misguided leaders for my Ummah."
"1167","Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa’d Sa’idi (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The outcome of deeds depends upon their ending.”"
"1168","This hadith is also narrated in the same way from Sayyiduna Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) through another chain of transmission."
"1169","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""An oath is either broken or one feels ashamed of it."
"1170","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""An oath is either broken or one feels ashamed of it."" Tabarani said: Only Abu Muawiyah has narrated it from Bashar, and we do not remember any other musnad hadith of Bashar besides this."
"1171","Alqamah bin Waqas says that I heard Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) say: ""Actions are based on intentions."" This hadith is brief."
"1172","Alqamah bin Waqas says that I heard Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, say that I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say... and he narrated this hadith."
"1173","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""All actions depend upon intentions, and for every person is what he intended. So, whoever's migration was for Allah and His Messenger, then his migration is indeed for Allah and His Messenger. And whoever's migration was for worldly gain or to marry a woman, then his migration is for that for which he migrated."
"1174","Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) received news that there was some discord among the Banu Amr bin Awf. Then he narrated this hadith, and in it was also that: “Clapping is for women.”"
"1175","Abu Abd Rabb al-Izzat says that I heard Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) saying on the pulpit that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Only trial and tribulation remain in the world, and the example of each of your deeds is like that of a vessel, if the upper part (of its drink) is pure, then the lower part will also be pure, and if the upper part is impure, then the lower part will also be impure."
"1176","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Suckling is only (established) by drinking milk due to hunger."" This hadith is concise."
"1177","This narration is also reported from Ash'ath through another chain; he narrated it, and in it is (the wording): ""Aisha! Make sure to see who your (milk) brothers are, for suckling is (established) through drinking milk in hunger."
"1178","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, these hearts become rusty just as iron becomes rusty."" It was asked: O Messenger of Allah! What is its polish (means of shining)? He said: ""Remembering death in abundance and recitation of the Qur'an."
"1179","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, these hearts become rusty just as iron becomes rusty."" It was asked: O Messenger of Allah! What is its polish (means of shining)? He said: ""Recitation of the Qur'an."
"1180","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) entered the mosque while supporting himself on me and was saying: ""Who among you would be pleased that Allah saves him from the steam of Hell?"" Then he said: ""Listen! Indeed, the deeds of Paradise are surrounded by severe and lofty hardships."" He said this three times. (Then he said:) ""Listen! Indeed, the deeds of Hell,"" or he said, ""the deeds of the world are surrounded by easy pleasures and desires."
"1181","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, vows and oaths are either broken or one becomes ashamed of them."
"1182","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Information is not like direct observation."
"1183","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Information is not like direct observation."
"1184","This hadith is also narrated in a similar manner through another chain from Hushaym with his chain. Yahya bin Hassan says that Hushaym did not hear this hadith."
"1185","Bahz bin Hakim narrates from his father, who narrates from his grandfather, that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no backbiting against a transgressor (fasiq)."
"1186","This narration is also reported through another chain from Ja'd bin Yahya with his chain in the same manner."
"1187","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The oppressor has no right to kinship."
"1188","Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Flattery is not found among the morals of a believer."
"1189","Sayyiduna Abu Humayd (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said while delivering a sermon: ""After death, there is no opportunity to seek repentance."
"1190","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated this hadith: ""No major sin remains with seeking forgiveness, and no minor sin remains minor with persistence."
"1191","Amr ibn Shu'aib narrates from his father, who narrates from his grandfather, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever imitates anyone other than us is not from among us, and do not imitate the Jews and Christians. The greeting of the Jews is to gesture with the fingers, while the greeting of the Christians is to gesture with the palms."
"1192","It is narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""He is not one of us whom Allah has granted (financial) abundance, yet he is miserly towards his family, while his (family members) smell fragrance from the neighbors, but the neighbors think that they are being clothed, whereas they are not being clothed."
"1193","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not recite the Qur'an with a pleasant voice is not from among us."
"1194","1194 - And I am Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Umar al-Tujibi, (he said): I was told by Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Jami‘ al-Sukkari, reading to him, (he said): I was told by Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghdadi, reading to him, (he said): I was told by Ishaq ibn Isma‘il, (he said): I was told by Sufyan, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Nahik, from Sa‘d ibn Abi Waqqas, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: « لَيْسَ مِنَّا مَنْ لَمْ يَتَغَنَّ بِالْقُرْآنِ » . Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz said: And this hadith was narrated by Waki‘ from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Abd Allah ibn al-Sa’ib, from Sa‘d, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. And it was also narrated by Waki‘, (he said): I was told by Sa‘id ibn Hassan al-Makhzumi, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Nahik, from Sa‘d, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: « لَيْسَ مِنَّا مَنْ لَمْ يَتَغَنَّ بِالْقُرْآنِ »"
"1195","Abdullah bin Naheek says that I heard Sayyiduna Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) narrate the hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in this manner."
"1196","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not recite the Qur'an with a pleasant voice is not from among us."" Imam Layth narrated this hadith in Egypt contrary to the narration that was reported in Iraq."
"1197","It is narrated from Saeed bin Abi Saeed that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever does not recite the Qur'an with a pleasant voice is not from among us."
"1198","Abdullah bin Sa’ib bin Nahik says that I went to Sayyiduna Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: Nephew! Who are you? When I told him, he said: Welcome, you are a trader who earns a living. How do you recite the Qur’an? I said: I recite well. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Recite the Qur’an and weep; if you cannot weep, then assume the appearance of one who is weeping, and recite the Qur’an with a pleasant voice, for whoever does not recite the Qur’an with a pleasant voice or does not try to recite it with a pleasant voice is not one of us.”"
"1199","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever does not recite the Qur'an with a pleasant voice is not from among us."
"1200","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says: ""Whoever does not recite the Qur'an with a pleasant voice is not one of us."
